## PID
id: pid-rule
type: reference

Data submitted to the HDI have PII. Full name, address, date of birth, and SSN are used in HiPER to produce the PID. These PIDs are extremely stable over time. Name changes and typos typically do not break a PID linkage because HiPER keeps a knowledge repository that is referenced when new data is PIDed. For every record that receives a PID a HashID is also included.

Because the PID is so stable it is the basis for MPID and the mother/child linkage roster.